<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>HTML List Types</title>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- 1. UNORDERED LIST (Bulleted) -->
    <h2>1. Unordered List (&lt;ul&gt;)</h2>
    <p>Used when the order of items does not matter:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>HTML</li>
        <li>CSS</li>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
    </ul>

    <hr>

    <!-- 2. ORDERED LIST (Numbered) -->
    <h2>2. Ordered List (&lt;ol&gt;)</h2>
    <p>Used when sequence or ranking matters:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Open VS Code</li>
        <li>Create an <code>index.html</code> file</li>
        <li>Write your HTML code</li>
        <li>Open the file in a browser</li>
    </ol>

    <!-- Optional attributes on <ol> -->
    <p>Ordered list using Roman numerals (<code>type="I"</code>) starting at 3 (<code>start="3"</code>):</p>
    <ol type="I" start="3">
        <li>Third Chapter</li>
        <li>Fourth Chapter</li>
    </ol>

    <hr>

    <!-- 3. DESCRIPTION LIST (Key-Value / Glossary) -->
    <h2>3. Description List (&lt;dl&gt;)</h2>
    <p>Used for terms and their definitions or descriptions:</p>
    <dl>
        <dt><strong>HTML</strong></dt>
        <dd>HyperText Markup Language — defines the structure of a webpage.</dd>

        <dt><strong>CSS</strong></dt>
        <dd>Cascading Style Sheets — controls the visual layout and styling.</dd>

        <dt><strong>DOM</strong></dt>
        <dd>Document Object Model — the browser's tree representation of the page.</dd>
    </dl>

    <hr>

    <!-- BONUS: NESTED LIST -->
    <h2>4. Nested List Example</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Frontend Technologies
            <ol>
                <li>Structure (HTML)</li>
                <li>Styling (CSS)</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li>Backend Technologies</li>
    </ul>

</body>

</html>